/-!
# ECTheoryLib

The public entry point for the domain library. General tools include additive
upper and lower bounds, variable drift, and multiplicative upper bounds. Problem
modules define objectives and optimality; algorithms supply exact transition PMFs
and invariants. Analysis modules instantiate these tools on actual path measures.

Completed analyses include binary and multivalued RLS, the uniform-initialization
logarithmic estimate, EA–OneMax bounds, coordinate-policy reuse, and full front coverage for SEMO/GSEMO including preferred-parent policies. Runtime uses
extended expectations and counts transitions after initialization. Fixed evaluation
costs are modeled separately. See the roadmap for analyses not yet completed.

Probability foundations reuse mathlib; this entry point does not import reference
snapshots or independent learning projects.
-/
